WEBVTT

00:34:29.042 --> 00:34:31.437
then you're not telling the full story.

00:34:31.461 --> 00:34:33.403
CA: I mean, what I hear you saying, Liz,

00:34:33.427 --> 00:34:35.304
is that you have written this new book.

00:34:35.328 --> 00:34:39.026
It's not directly from that
extraordinary dark night of the soul

00:34:39.050 --> 00:34:40.323
that you've been through.

00:34:40.347 --> 00:34:44.804
It's that you've been through
this process of healing and resilience,

00:34:44.828 --> 00:34:49.346
and that you've actually used this novel
in a way to be part of that healing,

00:34:49.370 --> 00:34:51.293
that the actual dedication to go there,

00:34:51.317 --> 00:34:53.493
to immerse yourself
in those original ideas

00:34:53.517 --> 00:34:55.059
has actually helped you.

00:34:55.083 --> 00:34:57.059
EG: Yeah, it was the healing.

00:34:57.083 --> 00:34:58.827
And the mistake that I was making --

00:34:58.851 --> 00:35:02.798
and I wouldn't have done that
if the book wasn't so ferociously due.